Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-01-2000||08:23 PM||||Well, I finally re-assembled my entire top-end.  I checked and double-checked all my fuel, vacuum, and coolant lines.... re-inserted fuel pump fuse, filled coolant, connected battery cable, and turned the key!  She cranked a few times while the fuel system re-pressurized, and BOOM!  I mean, VROOM!  No loose rockers, no exhuast leaks, no more smoke on startup, and my idle problem is magically gone(prolly vacuum leak.) I can't believe how good it sounds without that exhuast leak.  There was a little smoke from my oily fingers on the exhaust manifolds, but everything is cool.  In case you haven't been following, I tore it up so the heads could get ported, milled, and new seals.  Also, my exhaust manifold leak was fixed and both were ported as well.  I'm gonna set the timing and fix a couple odds and ends tomorrow.  I'll let you know if my a$$-o-meter shows an improvement!<P>-Mr. Bastard||||reg||14
Z||000001||fiero56||06-02-2000||01:29 AM||||Glad to hear it stared right up for you. That is always the most exciting moment. I have been following your questions etc, because I hope to install a 3.4 and, and your top end questions and answers will hopefully come in handy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||06-02-2000||01:50 AM||||Awesome, Keep it shinny side up! make sure to calibrate the a$$ O meter before you flog the ponys!||||reg||12
Z||000003||GT Bastard||06-02-2000||02:14 AM||||I'll be poppin' wheelies and burning rubber for you guys tomorrow!  Or not...  But it really isn't all that bad.  The crappy part for me was all those brackets on the right ride of the motor(passenger.)  There just isn't much clearance.  I was also really paranoid about getting the valves adjusted right, and luckily it's fine. All in all, it was a awesome learning experience.    <p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 06-02-2000).]||||reg||1
